        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Auction Forty-Fives',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Auction Forty-Fives (45s, Nova Scotia style) is a partnership trick game: 4 or 6 players, 5 cards each plus 4-card kitty. Bid in 5s (min 15-20); high bidder declares trump and may exchange with kitty. First team to 120 wins. Trump: 5 highest, then J, then A of hearts (always trump). Each trick 5 points; highest trump in trick +5. Special: 30 for 60 (win all tricks); 60 for 120 when below zero. Part of the Forty-Fives and Spoil Five family; regional rules vary.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Descendant of the Irish game Spoil Five; widely played among Irish communities in the New World, especially in Nova Scotia and the rest of Atlantic Canada.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 or 6 in partnerships (opposite). 5 cards each (3+2), 4-card kitty.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 cards. Trump: 5 high, then J, A of hearts always trump.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52-card deck; score to 120.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Left of dealer bids first; dealer may hold. High bidder names trump, may exchange with kitty.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Nova Scotia 45s: Standard rules as documented; bid in 5s, 120 to win.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
